...@classes

direction: down

title: The DAC tap - watching the box without fiber {
  near: top-center
  shape: text
  style: {font-color: "#727169"; font-size: 20; bold: true}
}

box: Fiber Box X6\n(no fiber attached)\nboots, thinks it talks to a LAN client {class: carrier}

cwwk: CWWK S8 {
  class: ours
  f0: SFP+ port 1 (enp1s0f0)\nWAS-110 - the real WAN {class: box}
  f1: SFP+ port 2 (enp1s0f1)\ntcpdump capture point {class: ours}
}

box -> cwwk.f1: DAC cable\ntwinax copper, no optics {style.stroke: "#98bb6c"; style.stroke-width: 2}

note: Can't tap XGS-PON (p2p, 10G, encrypted). But the box's 10G LAN port speaks\nplain Ethernet into an empty SFP+ cage.  tcpdump -ni enp1s0f1  ->  RIPv2 to 224.0.0.9 {
  near: bottom-center
  shape: text
  style: {font-color: "#e6c384"; font-size: 14; italic: true}
}
